ntent":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $f_1$, $f_2$, $f_3$, $\\dots$ be a sequence of numbers such that\n\\[\n  f_n = f_{n - 1} + f_{n - 2}\n\\]for every integer $n \\ge 3$.  If $f_7 = 83$, what is the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"15f9e6e33af29f08f5272d6d917c8a75e8f65becc78e49e0c1c1b49019488b42"},"seconds":65.39506220817566,"seed":637278349699967673,"stop":"eos","text":"Given the sequence \\( f_n = f_{n-1} + f_{n-2} \\) for \\( n \\ge 3 \\), and \\( f_7 = 83 \\), we are to find the sum of the first 10 terms of this sequence. Let's start by expressing the terms of the sequence in terms of \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\).\n\nFirst, we write the terms up to \\( f_7 \\):\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_3 &= f_2 + f_1, \\\\\nf_4 &= f_3 + f_2 = (f_2 + f_1) + f_2 = f_1 + 2f_2, \\\\\nf_5 &= f_4 + f_3 = (f_1 + 2f_2) + (f_2 + f_1) = 2f_1 + 3f_2, \\\\\nf_6 &= f_5 + f_4 = (2f_1 + 3f_2) + (f_1 + 2f_2) = 3f_1 + 5f_2, \\\\\nf_7 &= f_6 + f_5 = (3f_1 + 5f_2) + (2f_1 + 3f_2) = 5f_1 + 8f_2.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nGiven \\( f_7 = 83 \\), we have:\n\\[\n5f_1 + 8f_2 = 83.\n\\]\n\nWe now need to find the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence. The sum \\( S_{10} \\) is given by:\n\\[\nS_{10} = f_1 + f_2 + f_3 + f_4 + f_5 + f_6 + f_7 + f_8 + f_9 + f_{10}.\n\\]\n\nWe can express \\( f_8, f_9, \\) and \\( f_{10} \\) in terms of \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\):\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_8 &= f_7 + f_6 = (5f_1 + 8f_2) + (3f_1 + 5f_2) = 8f_1 + 13f_2, \\\\\nf_9 &= f_8 + f_7 = (8f_1 + 13f_2) + (5f_1 + 8f_2) = 13f_1 + 21f_2, \\\\\nf_{10} &= f_9 + f_8 = (13f_1 + 21f_2) + (8f_1 + 13f_2) = 21f_1 + 34f_2.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum \\( S_{10} \\) is:\n\\[\nS_{10} = f_1 + f_2 + (f_2 + f_1) + (f_1 + 2f_2) + (2f_1 + 3f_2) + (3f_1 + 5f_2) + (5f_1 + 8f_2) + (8f_1 + 13f_2) + (13f_1 + 21f_2) + (21f_1 + 34f_2).\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\\[\nS_{10} = (f_1 + f_1 + f_1 + 2f_1 + 3f_1 + 5f_1 + 8f_1 + 13f_1 + 21f_1) + (f_2 + f_2 + 2f_2 + 3f_2 + 5f_2 + 8f_2 + 13f_2 + 21f_2 + 34f_2) = 55f_1 + 88f_2.\n\\]\n\nSince \\( 5f_1 + 8f_2 = 83 \\), we can express \\( 55f_1 + 88f_2 \\) in terms of 83:\n\\[\n55f_1 + 88f_2 = 11(5f_1 + 8f_2) = 11 \\cdot 83 = 913.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence is \\(\\boxed{913}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{913}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
